-The absorption-only model renders a participating medium composed of cold, perfectly black particles that absorb all intercepted light without scattering or emitting [S1, unofficial][S4, book][S6]. It solves for light intensity attenuation along a ray, producing an X-ray-like projection or a "black smoke" obscuring a background [S4, book][S7, unofficial]. Unlike the [Emission-only Model](1016-emission-only-model.md) which adds radiance, or the [Single Scattering Model](1053-single-scattering-model.md) which redirects light, this model considers only the exponential decay of incident radiance [S3][S8].
